{"slug":"jim-kolbe","qid":"Q284704","name":"Jim Kolbe","desc":"American politician (1942–2022)","article":"Jim Kolbe","born":"1942-06-28","died":"2022-12-03","birthplace":"Evanston","parties":["Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"AZ-08","f":2003,"u":2007},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"AZ-05","f":1985,"u":2003},{"t":"Arizona State Senate","w":"","f":1977,"u":1982}],"summary":"James Thomas Kolbe (June 28, 1942 – December 3, 2022) was an American politician who served as a Republican member of the United States House of Representatives. He represented Arizona's 5th congressional district from 1985 to 2003 and its 8th congressional district from 2003 to 2007. A moderate, pro–abortion rights Republican, he came out as gay in 1996 after voting in support of the Defense of Marriage Act; his subsequent re-elections made him the second openly gay Republican elected to Congress.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2004,"o":"H","k":"AZ-08","p":"R","v":183363,"s":60.36,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":2002,"o":"H","k":"AZ-08","p":"R","v":126930,"s":63.33,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":172986,"s":60.15,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1998,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":103952,"s":51.6,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1996,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":179349,"s":68.74,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":149514,"s":67.72,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":172867,"s":66.54,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":138975,"s":64.75,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":164462,"s":67.8,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1986,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":119647,"s":64.85,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1984,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":116075,"s":50.92,"w":true,"n":"Jim Kolbe"},{"y":1982,"o":"H","k":"AZ-05","p":"R","v":80531,"s":48.28,"w":false,"n":"Jim Kolbe"}]}